## btleplug 0.13.3

The pinned Rust source is bundled in rust/vendor/btleplug. Local Apple lifecycle, Windows session ownership and Android service identity
changes are recorded in rust/vendor/btleplug.patch; original published
file hashes and reviewed overrides are in rust/vendor/btleplug-source.json.
These changes add owned Apple event tasks and adapter-thread shutdown/join, plus
Android service-scoped JNI calls and notification identities, and termination
on native notification transport/overflow errors. A result-bearing notification
API preserves terminal causes for the Dart event path. Windows partial device/session
initialization owns handler registrations, propagates PDU query errors and closes
the GATT session explicitly. Explicit Windows disconnect reports cleanup errors
and retains unfinished steps for retry; cancelled setup uses best-effort Drop.
Windows device and notification owners retire publication gates before handler
removal, joining library publication already in progress and rejecting late callbacks
even if WinRT removal fails. Windows discovery propagates metadata/descriptor
failures, caches validated attribute identity/properties and stages newly discovered
services before publication. GUID conversion uses fields directly. Windows
advertisement buffer queries propagate errors instead of panicking. Scan handlers
retain failed removal tokens, retire publication before stopping, and hold only
weak adapter-manager ownership; watcher destruction attempts stop and removal.
The five production WinRT event handlers catch Rust unwinding inside their foreign
callback entry points and return an HRESULT error while preserving ordinary errors.
JNI adapter entry points, including the generated connection-state wrapper, use a
local error policy that releases caught
panic payloads and secondary disposal panics while preserving Java exception
mapping. The JNI dependency itself is unmodified. The Android Rust peripheral also exposes the existing Java MTU request queue,
validates callback results, resets negotiation state on connect, and reports the
existing effective MTU for subsequent Android 14+ requests. The local notification extension uses subscribe_with_options and
unsubscribe_with_options with an explicit standard/compat setup policy. Android
compat skips the CCCD write; Apple still calls setNotifyValue. Existing standard
subscription behavior is retained. The upstream
Bluetooth implementation is retained. Linux sessions now own their D-Bus resource
task, abort and join it during explicit manager shutdown, and retain the task
handle across cancelled shutdown. Adapters and peripherals share that owner. Original license text follows.

Bundled Android Java changes are recorded in android/patches and
android/LOCAL-PATCHES.sha256, including lifecycle, service identity, API 33
event-value copying and queue overflow cause fixes. The Rust JNI stream preserves
Java exception text. android/UPSTREAM-SOURCES.sha256 records original bytes.

